(text "24 V BUS (red): bench supply + -> F0 -> VM on every driver. Ground return (black): every driver GND -> bench supply -" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 205.74 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0f9ed980-f6fd-486c-8eb8-427e7dfef989))
(text "NOTES\n1. Mega pins: STEP D22-26, DIR D30-34, EN D36-40 (LOW = driver on; 10k pull-ups keep drivers OFF while the Mega boots), encoders A0-A4, gripper PWM D9, tool I2C D20-D21.\n2. TMC2209 in UART mode: MS1/MS2 set each driver bus address (0-3), microsteps and current are set over UART by the firmware. CLK = GND selects the internal clock.\n3. Pin names follow BIGTREETECH TMC2209 V1.2/V1.3. UART is on pin 4 (factory default). Check against the silkscreen of the modules you buy. The trimmer is not used in UART mode.\n4. TMC2209 VM max is about 29 V: 24 V only. Never plug or unplug a motor with 24 V present. Verify coil pairs with an ohmmeter.\n5. Modules sit in female headers on perfboard, see carrier/. Heatsink on every module, 40 mm fan over the row.\n6. All grounds common. Never connect 24 V or 6 V to the Mega 5 V pins." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 40.64 535.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid 1b316e12-9e00-49bc-a9eb-38f8cd9c5591))
(text "BILL OF MATERIALS (electrical parts; full list, links and prices in hardware/bom)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 358.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid f904be8d-9df4-4839-b14e-29ed51408ef4))
(text "Ref\nU1\nPS2\nU2\nPS1\nDRV1-DRV5\nM1, M3\nM2\nM4\nM5\nM7\nJ6\nU6\nENC1-ENC5\nF0-F2\nSW1\nK1\nD1\nC7, C20-C24\nC1-C5, C8\nR1-R5, R13, R21-R25, R31-R32\nFAN1" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 155d05ca-72aa-4245-abd3-ec5cde7e9f7c))
(text "Qty\n1\n1\n1\n1\n5\n2\n1\n1\n1\n1\n1\n1\n5\n3\n1\n1\n1\n6\n6\n13\n1" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 60.96 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid ec9dab10-df34-4535-bb1b-2773f7dd5a9b))
(text "Part\nRaspberry Pi 5 8GB\nOfficial Raspberry Pi 27 W USB-C supply\nArduino Mega 2560 R3\n24 V supply\nBIGTREETECH TMC2209 V1.3 + heatsink\nSTEPPERONLINE 17HS19-1684S-PG5\nSTEPPERONLINE 17HS19-1684S-PG14\nSTEPPERONLINE 17HS08-1004S\nSTEPPERONLINE 11HS12-0674S\nMG996R servo\nGX12 6-pin tool plug\nXL4015 5 A buck module, set 6.0 V\nAS5600 magnetic encoder module + diametric magnet\nInline ATO fuse holders, 10 A, 2 A and 3 A fuses\nE-stop, 22 mm latching mushroom, 1 NC\n24 V coil relay, normally open, with socket\n1N4007 flyback diode\nElectrolytic 1000 uF 16 V (x1), 100 uF 35 V (x5)\nCeramic 100 nF\n1k (x8), 10k (x5) metal film 1/4 W\n40 mm 5 V fan over driver row" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 71.12 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 5e016c60-cd5d-4d25-860e-3359799a6cf5))
(text "Note\nowned\nowned\nowned\nowned\n\nJ1, J3\nJ2\nJ4\nJ5\nJ6 gripper tool\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 162.56 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 07a59cd9-abb3-47ff-a5ea-ef9d53c774b8))
